## Table: `Stock_Order` (`tblyezK6u6JsGu4cJ`)

| Field Name | Type | Notes |
|------------|------|-------|
| ID | Auto number | Primary field. |
| Order Id | Single line text | Mirrors `Unique_Orders` → `Order ID`. |
| Device type | Single line text | Item code selected in the app. |
| Date Ordered | Date | Calendar day captured from the form. |
| Quantity ordered / QTY dispatched | Numbers | Order vs. fulfilled quantity. |
| Contractor Company / Region / Technician | Single line text | Routing data. |
| Waybill number | Single line text | Courier reference. |
| Dispatch / order | Single select | Indicates whether the row represents a dispatch or pending order. |
| Dispatch to | Single line text | Destination contact/location. |
| Ordered by | Single line text | Email captured from the form. |
| Item Category / Description / Nature | Single line text | Mirrors the selected category and description. |
| Order Location | Single line text | Technician area / warehouse. |
| Status flags (Stock Availability, Pick Status, Dispatch Method) | Single select | Operational workflow metadata. |
| Recipient Name / Contact / Address | Text | Delivery details. |
| Deliver to Part | Single line text | Delivery party selection. |
| Dispatch Date | Date | Fulfillment tracking. |
| Notes, Attachments, Bill Folder | Text & Attachments | Optional supporting artefacts. |
| Related Unique Order | Linked record → `Unique_Orders` | Reverse link `Stock Order`. |
| Related Dispatch Log Entry | Linked record → `Dispatch_Log` | Reverse link `Stock Order`. |

**Usage**: Represents the core transactional table for order submissions. The React app currently writes new rows into this table via the Airtable API.

